 top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n304:## 3. Precision and layout\n318:## 4. What every adopted change has in common\n=== NEG ===\n12:## 1. The most expensive lesson: a fake +28 % that passed every gate\n33:## 2. Retired by measurement\n52:## 3. The negatives that were really instrumentation failures\n71:## 4. Conditionally retired — re-open after the draft-head fine-tune\n88:## 4b. Killed inside the winning iteration — the radix top-k's two dead levers (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n119:## 5. What the negatives taught","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
