{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeDoBb1UGe6es55wmoVf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The run is in Phase 1 of 6. I'll wait for the monitor rather than poll.\n\n**Status so far, iteration 3, ladder item 1.3 (`seq_len <= topk` early-out):**\n\n- **Implemented** — `include/topk_radix.h`: when `lim <= topk` the MSB-first threshold search is skipped whole and the gather runs with `thr = 0`. Threaded through all four `_rx` kernels as a launch argument; `DSV4_TOPK_EARLY=0` restores the full search on the same binary, so both A/B arms are one build.\n- **Unit gate PASS** — bit-identical to the untouched warp selection sort on 4 kernel shapes × 6 distributions × 13 lengths, with the early-out both ON and OFF. Kernel band: **+4.04 µs at T=384**, +3.90 at T=512, and **inert to within 0.05 µs above T=512** (the built-in negative control).\n- **In-situ gate PASS** — 12 PASS / 0 FAIL, ~1 M index slots memcmp'd against the warp reference on real score rows so far.\n- **Predicted engine effect: 0.064 %** (4.04 µs × 21 ratio-4 layers = 85 µs of a ~133 ms forward). I stated that in the script header before launching, not after: the tok/s sweep cannot resolve it against the 3.5 % spread, which is why the run also does a dprof pair — `i:topk` brackets the changed launch and should show ~18 %.\n\nRemaining: tok/s OFF/ON sweeps, dprof OFF/ON, LOSSLESS gate, then the ladder entry + wiki (`kernel-optimisations.md` if kept, `negative-results.md` if the engine-level number says it isn't worth the branch) and the commit."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":695,"cache_read_input_tokens":155347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":695},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fee